          %h4#applications Applications
          %h5#BPSCharges Higher conserved current algebras and BPS charge extensions
          %p
            By the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+WZW+terms"} geometry of physics – WZW terms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantization"} prequantization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L} \colon X \to \mathbf{B}^{p+1}U(1)_{conn}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^{p+2}(X)
            may be thought of as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+term"} parameterized WZW term
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
            field theory decribing the propagation of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-brane"} p-brane
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Under this perspective, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+field"} Hamiltonian vector field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+symmetry"} point symmetry
            of this sigma-model field theory and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+form"} Hamiltonian form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            is is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+current"} conserved current
            corresponding to this via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether%27s+theorem"} Noether's theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoissondgAlgebra"}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickey+bracket"} Dickey bracket
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoissondgAlgebra"}
            expresses the shift of currents by trivial currents (
            %a{:href => "#KS"}> KS
            ).
          %p
            Hence under this perspective, def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoissondgAlgebra"}
            gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            resolution of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickey+bracket"} Dickey bracket
            Lie algebra of conserved Noether currents for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+symmetries"} point symmetries
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+WZW+terms"} higher WZW sigma-models
            from gauge equivalence classes of conrved currents to the currents themselves.
          %p
            For the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetimes"} super spacetimes
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+form"} definite form
            on a super cocycle in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            then this is known as the algebra of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+charges"} BPS charges
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
